  nonce: 9de8  # 9de8
  message: "The 2026-09-17 fundamental concept audit of the pass-silence host boundary\nfound the mirror image of this row, and the two should be decided together.\n\nThis row: a pass that RAN (rust-analyzer's backend returned None) is filed as a\nSKIP. The audit found that for the 40 grammar-gated analyzers, a pass that\npartly ran BUILDS AN AnalysisRun -- times itself, appends the INV-pitab warning\nto it -- and collect_analyzer_result then discards it, because\nanalysis_runs.append sits only in the else of \"if is_skipped:\". Live repro in\nWI-gidid.\n\nThat matters for the choice this row poses between (a) stop marking it skipped\nand (b) declare a new axis value. It also re-frames ADR-0056 item 5, which this\nrow cites: the owner was asked whether an AnalysisRun should be EMITTED for a\npass that did not run. For the grammar-gated cohort the real question is\nwhether the one already CREATED should be KEPT -- a materially weaker case for\nthe ADR's ABSENT != EMPTY objection, since those passes did begin work.\n\nAlso relevant to the \"inflates the skip denominator\" point here: measured on\ncomponent-model-demo, 130 of 162 passes carry no_candidate_files, 48 via\nsilence_reason and 82 via skip_reason_code, and the host is chosen by\nLANGUAGE_EXTENSIONS membership and analyzer return style rather than by\nanything about the silence (WI-mamiv). So the denominator problem this row\nnames is not specific to rust-analyzer.\n\nNo action taken on this row. Status unchanged."  # 9de8
